Project: SnuggleFox's Games portfolio (static HTML/CSS/JS) with Convex-backed plays and total hours.

Purpose
- Showcase HTML game builds with click-to-play embeds.
- Track plays and total hours played via Convex.
- Provide a single game template (game/index.html) that loads by slug so new pages are not required.
- Offer a browse tile page and a separate About page.

Key Files
- index.html: Home page layout, loads games list from games.json.
- browse/index.html: Tile-only browse page for quick game selection.
- browse.js: Loads games.json, sorts by title, renders browse tiles.
- about/index.html: About page content and Discord contact button.
- game/index.html: Default game template; loads a game based on ?game=slug.
- styles.css: Global styling (dark warm tan theme + updated fonts).
- games.json: Single source of truth for games metadata, build paths, page URLs, and tile images.
- app.js: Loads games.json, sorts by updated date, renders cards on home page.
- game-cards.js: Renders each game card, handles click-to-play overlays, a single active game, and Convex play tracking.
- game-page.js: Loads a single game card by slug for game/index.html.
- convex-client.js: Convex cloud URL and HTTP query/mutation helpers.
- convex/schema.js: Play sessions and aggregate totals per game.
- convex/plays.js: Idempotent session saves and public totals query.
- supabase-client.js and supabase/schema.sql: Legacy references; no longer loaded by the pages.

Game Builds
- Live builds are hosted on itch.io as embed uploads.
- buildPath entries in games.json point to the itch.io embed-upload URL.

Adding or Updating a Game
1) Upload the HTML5 build to itch.io (embed upload).
2) Add/update the entry in games.json:
   - slug: URL-safe id (kebab-case)
   - title/description/tags/controls/updated
   - buildPath: itch.io embed-upload URL
   - pagePath: "/game/?game=<slug>"
   - tileImage: "images/<Image Name>" for browse tiles and play overlay poster (optional)

Click-to-Play Behavior
- The iframe uses data-src until clicked; clicking loads the build and starts play tracking.
- Only one game can be active at a time; activating a new game unloads the previous iframe and finalizes playtime.
- Clicking Play loads the game and requests fullscreen (or the existing mobile fullscreen view on touch devices). The Fullscreen button also toggles this view; iframe-initiated fullscreen remains blocked.

Convex Setup
- See README.md for deployment commands and tests.
- The frontend uses https://animated-curlew-362.convex.cloud, a development deployment.
- Deploy updates to this URL with CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:animated-curlew-362 and npx convex dev --once.
- Sessions save cumulative durations every 30 seconds and on lifecycle events; retries do not add plays or double-count time.

Hosting
- Site is hosted on GitHub Pages with a custom domain managed by Cloudflare DNS.
- Cloudflare DNS should use DNS-only records (no proxy) for GitHub Pages.
- GitHub Pages handles SSL after DNS propagates.

Local Dev
- games.json is loaded via fetch; the site must be served over http(s), not file://.
- Use a local web server (python, node, or any static server) when previewing.
- Update convex-client.js if switching to a different Convex deployment URL.

Notes
- The front page orders games by the updated field (newest first).
- Browse page sorts tiles alphabetically by title.
- Hours played shows total time across Convex play sessions. Legacy Supabase totals require a separate import.
